---
// The WebGL stage for the top page. Purely decorative — every word on the page
// lives in the sibling panels — so it is hidden from assistive tech. Until (or
// unless) the scene loads, the gradient underneath stands in for it.
//
// At boot the script lifts both of these elements out to <body>; see
// src/scripts/home-city.ts for why.
---
<div class="city-stage" data-city-stage aria-hidden="true">
  <div class="city-stage-fallback"></div>
  <canvas data-city-canvas></canvas>
</div>

<div class="city-hint" data-city-hint aria-hidden="true">
  <span>SCROLL</span><i></i>
</div>
